# Authentik applications

## Gate

Use when the user asks to list, inspect, create, update, or bind Authentik
**applications** (SSO app entries, launch URLs, icons, provider links). Skip
provider-only or flow-only asks (use those rules). Skip non-Authentik IdPs.

## Transport

No Authentik MCP was discovered for this harness. Prefer the Authentik
REST API with a resolved base URL and a short-lived API token from the
operator’s secret store / env (never hardcode hosts or paste tokens into
chat). If an Authentik MCP appears later, use its list/describe tools when
ready — **do not invent MCP tool names**.

Resolve base URL from operator config / env (for example
`AUTHENTIK_URL`) — never invent an internal hostname.

Auth header shape (token value never echoed):

```text
Authorization: Bearer <token>
Accept: application/json
```

## Resolve ids

Never invent application `pk`, `slug`, or `name`. Resolve from the user,
a prior list this turn, or:

| Need | API (relative to base) |
| --- | --- |
| List apps | `GET /api/v3/core/applications/` |
| Get by slug | `GET /api/v3/core/applications/{slug}/` |
| Search | `GET /api/v3/core/applications/?search=TERM` |
| Bound provider | read `provider` / `provider_obj` on the app detail |

If several match, list candidates (name + slug + provider name) and ask
once — do not pick the production app by vibes.

## Receipt shape

Report: **name**, **slug**, **provider name/type** (when bound), launch
URL host path only when useful. Never paste client secrets, API tokens,
or session cookies.

## Craft (gated create/update)

Create / update / rebind provider need an **explicit verb** this turn
naming the application (or create intent). Prefer update-in-place over
delete+recreate.

| Action | API shape |
| --- | --- |
| Create app | `POST /api/v3/core/applications/` with name, slug, provider pk |
| Patch app | `PATCH /api/v3/core/applications/{slug}/` |
| Bind provider | set `provider` to a pk resolved via `authentik-providers` |

Slug rules: lowercase, stable, no spaces. Do not rotate slug casually —
downstream bookmarks and reverse-proxy paths may depend on it.

Delete / disable → `authentik-safety` plus an explicit delete/disable
verb naming the slug.

## Groups / users (inventory only)

When the ask is “who can access this app,” list groups bound via policy /
group membership using:

| Need | API |
| --- | --- |
| List groups | `GET /api/v3/core/groups/` |
| Group detail | `GET /api/v3/core/groups/{group_uuid}/` |
| Users (metadata) | `GET /api/v3/core/users/?search=TERM` |

Report group **name** + member **count** (or usernames when asked). Never
dump passwords, TOTP, or recovery codes. Broadening membership is a
mutate — follow `authentik-safety`.

## Defaults

1. Read-only list/get is the default.
2. Resolve provider pk from `authentik-providers` before binding.
3. Cap paginated lists; summarize and offer a tighter `search=`.
4. Edge reverse-proxy / ingress wiring is out of scope — own the IdP app
   object only.
5. After an authorized mutate, re-GET the slug and report the new binding.

## Refuse

- Inventing application pks, slugs, or provider foreign keys.
- Pasting client secrets, tokens, or user passwords into chat.
- Claiming an app exists without a list/get this turn.
- Absorbing Keycloak / Authelia / generic OIDC products here.
